  "parsed_answer": "Yes. **rs6152 is a protein-coding variant** in the **AR (androgen receptor)** gene.\n\n- **Variant type:** it is a **synonymous coding SNP** in AR, historically known as **c.1050G>A (p.Glu350=)** in the canonical transcript.\n- **Protein-domain assignment:** because it is **synonymous**, it **does not change the amino acid sequence** of AR.\n- **Therefore, no AR protein region or domain is directly affected at the protein level.**\n\nSo, while rs6152 is **located in a coding exon**, it **is not an amino-acid-altering variant**, and a **protein-domain impact is not applicable**.",
